          %h3#OmegaSpectra Omega-spectra
          %p
            In order to motivate
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Omega-spectra"} Omega-spectra
            consider the following shadow of the structure they will carry:
          #BlueprintForIdeaOfOmegaSpectra.num_example
            %h6#example_6 Example
            %p
              A
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+abelian+group"} graded abelian group
              is equivalently a sequence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{A_n\}_{n \mathbb{Z}}
              of
              = succeed "-graded" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_n
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi n
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    A_n \simeq A_{n+1}[1]
                    \\,,
            %p
              (where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [1]
              denotes the operation of shifting all entries in a graded abelian group down in degree by -1). Because this means that the sequence of
              = succeed "-graded" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi ⋮
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi ⋮
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi a
                              %mn 3
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi a
                              %mn 2
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi a
                              %mn 1
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi ⋯
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
