              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:AdjunctStructureMaps"} (1)
              are
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalences"} weak homotopy equivalences
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi σ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [S^1, \tilde \sigma_n]_\ast
              is an isomorphism (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#UniversalPropertyOfHomotopyCategoryOfAModelCategory"}> prop.
              ). Therefore, by prop.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TwoVersionsOfComponentsForStableHomotopyGroupsAgree"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequential+colimit"} sequential colimit
              in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StableHomotopyGroups"}
              is entirely over isomorphisms and hence is given already by the first object of the sequence.
          %p We now show that every sequential pre-spectrum may be completed to an Omega-spectrum, up to stable weak homotopy equivalence:
          #SpectrificationForTopologicalSequentialSpectra.num_defn
            %h6#definition_8 Definition
