                    \\,.
            %p
              See for instance (
              %a{:href => "spectrification#LewisMaySteinberger86"}> Lewis-May-Steinberger 86, p. 3
              ) and (
              %a{:href => "spectrification#Weibel94"}> Weibel 94, 10.9.6 and topology exercise 10.9.2
              ).
          %h3#TopologicalDiagramsSequentialSpectra As topological diagrams
          %p
            In order to conveniently understand the stable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            structure on spectra, we now consider an equivalent reformulation of the component-wise definition of sequential spectra, def.
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SequentialSpectra"}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topologically+enriched+functors"} topologically enriched functors
            (
            %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#TopologicallyEnrichedFunctor"}> defn.
            ).
          #CategoriesOfStandardSpheres.num_defn
            %h6#definition_9 Definition
            %p Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ι
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi StdSpheres
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cg
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\iota \;\colon\; StdSpheres \longrightarrow Top_{cg}^{\ast/}
            %p
              for the non-full
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topologically+enriched+category"} topologically enriched
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcategory"} subcategory
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#TopEnrichedCategory"}> def.
              ) of that of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+topological+spaces"} pointed
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+topological+spaces"} compactly generated topological spaces
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#TopkAsATopologicallyEnrichedCategory"}> def.
              ) where:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
                  are the standard
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-spheres"} n-spheres
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^n
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi ℕ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smash+product"} smash product
                  powers
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mi n
                        %mo ≔
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mn 1
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mo ∧
                              %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^n \coloneqq (S^1)^{\wedge^n}
                  of the standard circle;
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-spaces"} hom-spaces
                  are
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi StdSpheres
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mi n
                        %mo ,
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mrow
                            %mi k
                            %mo +
                            %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≔
                        %mrow
                          %mo {
                          %mrow
                            %mtable
                              %mtr
                                %mtd
                                  %mo *
                                %mtd
                                  %mi for
                                %mtd
                                  %mi k
                                  %mo &lt;
                                  %mn 0
                              %mtr
                                %mtd
                                  %msup
                                    %mi S
                                    %mi k
                                %mtd
                                  %mi otherwise
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        StdSpheres(S^{n}, S^{k+n})
                        \\coloneqq
                        \\left\{
                        \\array{
                        \\ast &amp; for &amp; k \lt 0
                        \\\
                        S^k
                        \&amp; otherwise
                        }
                        \\right.
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
                  is induced from composition in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi Top
                          %mi cg
                          %mrow
                            %mo *
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top^{\ast/}_{cg}
                  by regarding the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-space"} hom-space
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^k
                  above as its
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Maps
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mi n
                        %mo ,
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mrow
                            %mi k
                            %mo +
                            %mi n
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo *
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Maps({S^n},S^{k+n})_\ast
                  under the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunct"} adjunct
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi k
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                    %mi Maps
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo +
                        %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    S^{k} \stackrel{}{\to} Maps({S^n},S^{k+n})_\ast
            %p of the canonical isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi k
                    %mo ∧
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi n
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo +
                        %mi n
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    S^k \wedge S^n \overset{\simeq}{\longrightarrow} S^{k+n}
                    \\,.
            %p This induces the category
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi StdSpheres
                    %mo ,
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cg
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [StdSpheres, Top^{\ast/}_{cg}]
            %p
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topologically+enriched+functors"} topologically enriched functors
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi StdSpheres
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} StdSpheres
              with values in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cg
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_{cg}^{\ast/}
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#TopologicallyEnrichedFunctorsToTopk"}> exmpl.
              ).
          #SequentialSpectraAsDiagramSpectra.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_6 Proposition
            %p
              There is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi seq
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi StdSpheres
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cg
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo ≃
                    %mi SeqSpec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cg
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (-)^seq
                    \\;\colon\;
                    [StdSpheres,\; Top_{cg}^{\ast/}]
                    \\overset{\simeq}{\longrightarrow}
                    SeqSpec(Top_{cg})
            %p
              from the category of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topologically+enriched+functors"} topologically enriched functors
              on the category of standard spheres of def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CategoriesOfStandardSpheres"}
              to the category of topological sequential spectra, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SequentialSpectra"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi StdSpheres
                    %mo ,
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cg
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in [StdSpheres,Top_{cg}^{\ast/}]
              to the sequential prespectrum
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mi seq
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^{seq}
              with components
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                      %mi seq
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X^{seq}_n \coloneqq X(S^n)
            %p and with structure maps
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ∧
                        %msubsup
                          %mi X
                          %mi n
                          %mi seq
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi σ
                              %mi n
                        %msubsup
                          %mi X
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo +
                            %mn 1
                          %mi seq
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi Maps
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msubsup
                          %mi X
                          %mi n
                          %mi seq
                        %mo ,
                        %msubsup
                          %mi X
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo +
                            %mn 1
                          %mi seq
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\frac{
                    S^1 \wedge X^{seq}_n \stackrel{\sigma_n}{\longrightarrow} X^{seq}_{n+1}
                    }{
                    S^1 \longrightarrow Maps(X^{seq}_n, X^{seq}_{n+1})_\ast
                    }
            %p
              being the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunct"} adjunct
              of the component map of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              on spheres of consecutive dimension.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_6 Proof
            %p
              First observe that from its components on maps of consecutive spheres the functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is already uniquely determined. Indeed, by definition the hom-space between non-consecutive spheres
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi StdSpheres
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} StdSpheres(S^n, S^{n+k})
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smash+product"} smash product
              of the hom-spaces between the consecutive spheres, for instance:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mn 1
                            %mo ∧
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %mi StdSpheres
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mi n
                            %mo ,
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo +
                                %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ∧
                            %mi StdSpheres
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo +
                                %mn 1
                            %mo ,
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo +
                                %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mo ≃
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mo ≃
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mo ∘
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mn 2
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %mi StdSpheres
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mi n
                            %mo ,
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo +
                                %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    S^1 \wedge S^1 &amp; = &amp; StdSpheres(S^n, S^{n+1}) \wedge StdSpheres(S^{n+1}, S^{n+2})
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{\simeq}}\downarrow
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    {}^{\mathllap{\simeq}}\downarrow^{\circ}
                    \\\
                    S^2 &amp; = &amp; StdSpheres(S^n , S^{n+2})
                    }
                    \\,,
            %p and so functoriality completely fixes the former by the latter.
            %p This means that we actually have a bijection between classes of objects.
            %p
              Now observe that a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to Y
              between two functors on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi StdSpheres
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} StdSpheres
              is equivalently a collection of component maps
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mi n
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi Y
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_n \colon X_n \to Y_n
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s \in S^1
              then the following squares commute
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi f
                                  %mi n
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi X
                                    %mrow
                                      %msup
                                        %mi S
                                        %mi n
                                      %mo ,
                                      %msup
                                        %mi S
                                        %mrow
                                          %mi n
                                          %mo +
                                          %mn 1
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi s
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi Y
                                    %mrow
                                      %msup
                                        %mi S
                                        %mi n
                                      %mo ,
                                      %msup
                                        %mi S
                                        %mrow
                                          %mi n
                                          %mo +
                                          %mn 1
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi s
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo +
                                %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi f
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi n
                                    %mo +
                                    %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo +
                                %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X(S^n)
                    \&amp;\overset{f_n}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    Y(S^{n})
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{X_{S^n,S^{n+1}}(s)}}\downarrow
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{Y_{S^n,S^{n+1}}(s)}}
                    \\\
                    X(S^{n+1})
                    \&amp;\underset{f_{n+1}}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    Y(S^{n+1})
                    }
                    \\,,
            %p By the smash/hom adjunction, the square equivalently factors as
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi f
                                  %mi n
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi s
                                  %mo ,
                                  %mi id
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi s
                                  %mo ,
                                  %mi id
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mn 1
                            %mo ∧
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mi id
                                %mo ×
                                %msub
                                  %mi f
                                  %mi n
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mn 1
                            %mo ∧
                            %mi Y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msubsup
                                    %mi σ
                                    %mi n
                                    %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msubsup
                                    %mi σ
                                    %mi n
                                    %mi Y
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo +
                                %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi f
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi n
                                    %mo +
                                    %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo +
                                %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X(S^n)
                    \&amp;\overset{f_n}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    Y(S^{n})
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{(s,id)}}\downarrow
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{(s,id)}}
                    \\\
                    S^1 \wedge X(S^n)
                    \&amp;\underset{id \times f_n}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    S^1 \wedge Y(S^n)
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{\sigma^X_n}}
                    \\downarrow
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{\sigma^Y_n}}
                    \\\
                    X(S^{n+1})
                    \&amp;\underset{f_{n+1}}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    Y(S^{n+1})
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              Here the top square commutes in any case, and so the total rectangle commutes precisely if the lower square commutes, hence if under our identification the components
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{f_n\}
              constitute a homomorphism of sequential spectra.
            %p Hence we have an isomorphism on all hom-sets, and hence an equivalence of categories.
          %p
            Further
            %a{:href => "#StrictModelStructureOnSequentialSpectra"} below
            we use prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SequentialSpectraAsDiagramSpectra"}
            to naturally induce a model structure on the category of topological sequential spectra.
          #TensoringOfSeqSpectraOverSpacesAsSpecialCaseOfTensoringTopologicalFunctors.num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              Under the equivalence of prop.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SequentialSpectraAsDiagramSpectra"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topologically+enriched+functors"} topologically enriched functors
              over topological spaces (according to
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#TensoringAndPoweringOfTopologicallyEnrichedCopresheaves"} this def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TensoringAndPoweringOfSequentialSpectra"}
          #LimitsAndColimitsOfSequentialSpectra.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_7 Proposition
            %p
              The category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SeqSpec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cq
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SeqSpec(Top_{cq})
              of sequential spectra (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SequentialSpectra"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
            %p Given
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi I
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi SeqSpec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cg
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X_\bullet
                    \\;\colon\;
                    I
                    \\longrightarrow
                    SeqSpec(Top_{cg})
            %p
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
              of sequential spectra, then:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  its colimiting spectrum has component spaces the colimit of the component spaces formed in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Top
                          %mi cg
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_{cg}
                  (via
                  %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#DescriptionOfLimitsAndColimitsInTop"} this prop.
                  and
                  = succeed "):" do
                    %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#kTopIsCoreflectiveSubcategory"} this corollary
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %munder
                            %mi lim
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mi i
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi n
                        %mo ≃
                        %msub
                          %munder
                            %mi lim
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mi i
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi i
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi n
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ,
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        (\underset{\longrightarrow}{\lim}_i X(i))_n
                        \\simeq
                        \\underset{\longrightarrow}{\lim}_i X(i)_n
                        \\,,
              %li
                %p
                  its limiting spectrum has component spaces the limit of the component spaces formed in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Top
                          %mi cg
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_{cg}
                  (via
                  %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#DescriptionOfLimitsAndColimitsInTop"} this prop.
                  and
                  = succeed "):" do
                    %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#kTopIsCoreflectiveSubcategory"} this corollary
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %munder
                            %mi lim
                            %mo ⟵
                          %mi i
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi n
                        %mo ≃
                        %msub
                          %munder
                            %mi lim
                            %mo ⟵
                          %mi i
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi i
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi n
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ;
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        (\underset{\longleftarrow}{\lim}_i X(i))_n
                        \\simeq
                        \\underset{\longleftarrow}{\lim}_i X(i)_n
                        \\,;
            %p moreover:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  the colimiting spectrum has structure maps in the sense of def.
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SequentialSpectra"}
                  given by
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
