          #StrictModelStructureOnSequentialPrespectraIsModelCategory.num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              The classes of morphisms in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ClassesOfMorphismsOfTheStrictModelStructureOnSequentialSpectra"}
              give the structure of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#ModelCategory"}> def.
              ) to be denoted
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SeqSpec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Top
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi strict
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SeqSpec(Top)_{strict}
              and called the
              %strong
                strict
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+topological+sequential+spectra"} model structure on topological sequential spectra
              (or:
              = succeed ")." do
                %strong level model structure
            %p
              Moreover, this is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrantly+generated+model+category"} cofibrantly generated model category
              with generating (acyclic) cofibrations the set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi I
                      %mi seq
                      %mi strict
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I_{seq}^{strict}
              (resp.
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi J
                        %mi seq
                        %mi strict
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J_{seq}^{strict}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GeneratingAndGeneratingAcyclicCofibrationsForSeqSpecStrict"}
          .proof
            %h6#proof_11 Proof
            %p
              Prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SequentialSpectraAsDiagramSpectra"}
              says that the category of sequential spectra is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalently
              an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functor+category"} enriched functor category
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SeqSpec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Top
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi StdSpheres
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cg
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    SeqSpec(Top)
                    \\simeq
                    [StdSpheres,\; Top_{cg}^{\ast/}]
                    \\,.
            %p
              Accordingly, this carries the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+model+structure+on+functors"} projective model structure on functors
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#ProjectiveModelStructureOnTopologicalFunctors"}> thm.
              ). This immediately gives the statement for the fibrations and the weak equivalences.
            %p
              It only remains to check that the cofibrations are as claimed. To that end, consider a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+square"} commuting square
              of sequential spectra
            .maruku-equation
