                    \\\
                    S^1 \wedge Y_n &amp;\stackrel{\sigma_n^Y}{\longrightarrow}&amp; Y_{n+1}
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \searrow &amp;&amp; \searrow
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; S^1 \wedge B_n &amp;\stackrel{\sigma_n^B}{\longrightarrow}&amp; B_{n+1}
                    }
                    \\;\;\;
                    \=
                    \\;\;\;
                    \\array{
                    S^1 \wedge X_n &amp;\stackrel{\sigma_n^X}{\longrightarrow}&amp; X_{n+1}
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \searrow^{\mathrlap{S^1 \wedge h_n}} &amp;&amp; \searrow^{\mathrlap{h_{n+1}}}
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; S^1 \wedge A_n &amp;\stackrel{\sigma_n^A}{\longrightarrow}&amp; A_{n+1}
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; S^1 \wedge B_n &amp;\stackrel{\sigma_n^B}{\longrightarrow}&amp; B_{n+1}
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              Hence a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lifting"} lifting
              in the original diagram is a lifting in each degree
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n+1
              makes these diagrams of structure maps commute.
            %p
              Since components are parameterized over
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/induction"} induction
            %p
              First of all there must be an ordinary lifting in degree 0. Since the strict fibrations are degreewise classical fibrations, this gives the condition that for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_\bullet
              to be a strict cofibration, then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_0
              is to be a classical cofibration.
            %p
              Then assume that a lifting
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi l
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} l_n
              in degree
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              has been found
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi n
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi h
                                  %mi n
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mi n
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi f
                                    %mi n
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↗
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi l
                                    %mi n
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
