              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-approximation"} CW-approximation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi n
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_{k \leq n} \colon  \hat X_{k \leq n} \to X_{k \leq n}
              has been found such that all the structure maps in degrees
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lt n
              are respected. Consider then the composite continuous function
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ∧
                    %msub
