                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi I
                          %mo +
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi SeqSpec
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ∧
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi I
                          %mo +
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi Y
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\frac{
                    I_+ \longrightarrow SeqSpec(X,Y)
                    }{
                    X \wedge (I_+) \longrightarrow Y
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              By prop.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CylinderSpectrumOverCWSpectrumIsGood"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-spectrum"} CW-spectrum
              then the standard
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cylinder+spectrum"} cylinder spectrum
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∧
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \wedge (I_+)
              is a good cyclinder object (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#PathAndCylinderObjectsInAModelCategory"}> def.
              ) on a cofibrant object.
            %p
              Since moreover every object in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SeqSpec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cg
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi strict
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SeqSpec(Top_{cg})_{strict}
              is fibrant, the statement follows (with
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#HomsOutOfCofibrantIntoFibrantComputeHomotopyCategory"} this lemma
          %h2#StableModelStructureOnSequentialSpectra The stable model structure on sequential spectra
          %p
            The actual spectrum objects of interest in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"} stable homotopy theory
            are not the pre-spectra of def.
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SequentialSpectra"}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Omega-spectra"} Omega-spectra
            of def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OmegaSpectrum"}
            among them. Hence we need to equip the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequential+pre-spectra"} sequential pre-spectra
            of def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SequentialSpectra"}
            with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model structure
            (
            %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#ModelCategory"}> def.
            ) whose fibrant-cofibrant objects are, in particular
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Omega-spectra"} Omega-spectra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Omega-spectrum"} Omega-spectrum
            and a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-spectrum"} CW-spectrum
            as in def.
            = succeed "." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CWSpectrum"}
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CellSpectraAreCofibrantInModelStructureOnTopologicalSequentialSpectra"}
            this suggests to construct a model category structure on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SeqSpec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Top
                    %mi cg
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SeqSpec(Top_{cg})
            that has the same cofibrations as the strict model structure of theorem
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StrictModelStructureOnSequentialPrespectraIsModelCategory"}
          %p
            Such a situation is called a
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} Bousfield localization of a model category
          %h3#bousfield_localization Bousfield localization
          %p
            In plain
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+localization"} reflective localization
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            is equivalently a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mi loc
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  i
                  \\;\colon\;
                  \\mathcal{C}_{loc}
                  \\hookrightarrow
                  \\mathcal{C}
          %p
            such that the inclusion functor has a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mi loc
                  %munderover
                    %mo ⊥
                    %munder
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi i
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟵
                      %mi L
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathcal{C}_{loc}
                  \\underoverset
                  {\underset{i}{\longrightarrow}}
                  {\overset{L}{\longleftarrow}}
                  {\bot}
                  \\mathcal{C}
                  \\,.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction+unit"} adjunction unit
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi η
                    %mi X
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi L
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_X \colon X \to L(X)
            “reflects” every object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            into one in the
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mi loc
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_{loc}
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategory"} reflective subcategory
            inclusion.
          %p
            It is a classical fact (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Calculus+of+fractions+and+homotopy+theory"}> Gabriel-Zisman 67
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "reflective+subcategory#CharacterizationByLocalization"} prop.
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mi loc
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msubsup
                    %mi W
                    %mi L
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathcal{C}_{loc}
                  \\simeq
                  \\mathcal{C}[W^{-1}_L]
          %p
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalently
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} localization
            (
            %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#HomotopyCategoryOfACategoryWithWeakEquivalences"}> def.
            ) of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            at the “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            \-equivalences”, namely at those morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L(f)
            is an isomorphism. Hence one also speaks of
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+localizations"} reflective localizations
          %p
            The following concept of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} Bousfield localization of model categories
            is the evident lift of this concept of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+localization"} reflective localization
            from the realm of categories to the realm of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+categories"} model categories
            (
            %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#ModelCategory"}> def.
            ), where isomorphism is generealized to weak equivalence and where
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functors"} adjoint functors
            are taken to exhibit
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunctions"} Quillen adjunctions
          #BousfieldLocalizationOfModelCategories.num_defn
            %h6#definition_18 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} left Bousfield localization
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mi loc
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_{loc}
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#ModelCategory"}> def.
              ) is another model category structure on the same underlying category with the same cofibrations,
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Cof
                      %mi loc
                    %mo =
                    %mi Cof
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Cof_{loc} = Cof
            %p but more weak equivalences
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mi loc
                    %mo ⊃
                    %mi W
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    W_{loc} \supset W
                    \\,.
          %p Notice that:
          #BasicPropertiesOfLectBousfieldLocalizations.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_21 Proposition
            %p
              Given a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} left Bousfield localization
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mi loc
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_{loc}
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              as in def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#BousfieldLocalizationOfModelCategories"}
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Fib
                          %mi loc
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi Fib
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Fib_{loc} \subset Fib
                  ;
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi W
                          %mi loc
                        %mo ∩
                        %msub
                          %mi Fib
                          %mi loc
                        %mo =
                        %mi W
                        %mo ∩
                        %mi Fib
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W_{loc} \cap Fib_{loc} = W \cap Fib
                  ;
              %li
                %p
                  the identity functors constitute a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen adjunction
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mi loc
                        %munderover
                          %mo ⊥
                          %munder
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mi id
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟵
                            %mi id
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\mathcal{C}_{loc}
                        \\underoverset
                        {\underset{id}{\longrightarrow}}
                        {\overset{id}{\longleftarrow}}
                        {\bot}
                        \\mathcal{C}
                        \\,.
              %li
                %p
                  the induced adjunction of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functors"} derived functors
                  (
                  %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#QuillenAdjunctionInducesAdjunctionOnHomotopyCategories"}> prop.
                  ) exhibits a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategory"} reflective subcategory
                  inclusion of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category+of+a+model+category"} homotopy categories
                  (
                  %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#HomotopyCategoryOfAModelCategory"}> def.
                  )
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Ho
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mi loc
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %munderover
                          %mo ⊥
                          %munder
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mi id
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟵
                            %mrow
                              %mi 𝕃
                              %mi id
                        %mi Ho
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        Ho(\mathcal{C}_{loc})
                        \\underoverset
                        {\underset{\mathbb{R} id}{\longrightarrow}}
                        {\overset{\mathbb{L}id}{\longleftarrow}}
                        {\bot}
                        Ho(\mathcal{C})
                        \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_21 Proof
            %p Regarding the first two items:
            %p
              Using the properties of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+factorization+systems"} weak factorization systems
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#WeakFactorizationSystem"}> def.
              ) of (acyclic cofibrations, fibrations) and (cofibrations, acyclic fibrations) for both model structures we get
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Fib
                              %mi loc
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi Cof
                              %mi loc
                            %mo ∩
                            %msub
                              %mi W
                              %mi loc
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi Inj
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⊂
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi Cof
                              %mi loc
                            %mo ∩
                            %mi W
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi Inj
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mi Fib
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    Fib_{loc}
                    \&amp;=
                    (Cof_{loc} \cap W_{loc})Inj
                    \\\
                    \&amp;\subset
                    (Cof_{loc} \cap W)Inj
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    Fib
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Fib
                              %mi loc
                            %mo ∩
                            %msub
                              %mi W
                              %mi loc
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %msub
                              %mi Cof
                              %mi loc
                            %mi Inj
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mi Cof
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mi Inj
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mi Fib
                            %mo ∩
                            %mi W
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    Fib_{loc} \cap W_{loc}
                    \&amp; =
                    Cof_{loc} Inj
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    Cof \, Inj
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    Fib \cap W
                    \\end{aligned}
                    \\,.
            %p Regarding the third point:
            %p
              By construction,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi id
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mi loc
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} id \colon \mathcal{C} \to \mathcal{C}_{loc}
              preserves cofibrations and acyclic cofibrations, hence is a left Quillen functor.
            %p Regarding the fourth point:
            %p
              Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Cof
                      %mi loc
                    %mo =
                    %mi Cof
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cof_{loc} = Cof
              the notion of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+homotopy"} left homotopy
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mi loc
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_{loc}
              is the same as that in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Fib
                      %mi loc
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi Fib
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Fib_{loc} \subset Fib
              by the first statement, on these cofibrant-fibrant objects the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+derived+functor"} right derived functor
              of the identity is just the identity and hence does exhibit this inclusion. The left adjoint to this inclusion is given by
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝕃
                      %mi id
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{L}id
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#QuillenAdjunctionInducesAdjunctionOnHomotopyCategories"} prop
          %p
            In plain
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
