              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
              because the adjunction unit and counit are stable weak equivalences.
          %p With this in hand, we now finally state the comparison between standard and alternative suspension:
          #IsomorphismBetweenStandardAndAlternativeSuspensionInHomotopyCategory.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma_12 Lemma
            %p
              There is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category+of+a+model+category"} homotopy category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi SeqSpec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cg
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi stable
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(SeqSpec(Top_{cg})_{stable})
              of the stable model structure, between the total
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functors"} derived functors
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#QuillenAdjunctionInducesAdjunctionOnHomotopyCategories"}> prop.
              ) of the standard suspension (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SequentialSpectrumRealSuspension"}
              = succeed "):" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SequentialSpectrumFakeSuspension"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∧
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
