            %h6#proof_38 Proof
            %p
              By prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AlternativeSuspensionIsLeftQuillenOnStrictModelStructureOnSequential"}
              and the fact that the stable model structure has the same cofibrations as the strict model structure,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
              preserves stable cofibrations. Moreover, by lemma
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FakeLoopingPreservesOmegaSpectra"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
              preserves in fact all stable weak equivalences. Hence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
              is a left Quillen functor and so
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\Sigma \dashv \Omega)
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen adjunction
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FakeSuspensionInducesEquivalenceOfHomotopyCategories"}
              gives that this Quillen adjunction is a Quillen equivalence.
          %p
            In summary, this concludes the characterization of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+category"} stable homotopy category
            as the result of stabilizing the canonical
            = succeed "-adjunction" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\Sigma \dashv \Omega)
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+homotopy+category"} classical homotopy category
          #StableHomotopyCategoryIsIndeedStabilizationOfClassicalHomotopyCategory.num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_4 Theorem
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+pointed+topological+spaces"} classical model structure
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cg
