                        %mi seq
                        %mi stable
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J_{seq}^{stable}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+cell+complexes"} relative cell complexes
              are precisely the stable acyclic cofibrations.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_45 Proof
            %p
              Since all elements of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi J
                      %mi seq
                      %mi stable
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J_{seq}^{stable}
              are stable weak equivalences and strict cofibrations by lemma
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ElementsOfKAreStableEquivalencesAndStrictCofibrationsForSequentialSpectra"}
              = succeed "-cell" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi J
                        %mi seq
                        %mi stable
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J_{seq}^{stable}
            %p
              In the other direction, let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              be a stable acyclic cofibration. Apply the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+object+argument"} small object argument
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#SmallObjectArgument"}> prop.
              ) to factor it
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %munderover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi J
                          %mi seq
                          %mi stable
                        %mi Cell
                      %mi i
                    %munderover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi J
                          %mi seq
                          %mi stable
                        %mi Inj
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f \colon \underoverset{J_{seq}^{stable}Cell}{i}{\to}
                    \\underoverset{J_{seq}^{stable} Inj}{p}{\to}
            %p
