          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_10 Remark
            %p
              Prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SemiaddtiveStructureUnderlyingAdditiveInducesOriginalEnrichment"}
              says that being an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/additive+category"} additive category
              is an extra
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/property"} property
              on a category, not extra
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
          %p In conclusion we have:
          #TheStableHomotopyCategoryIsAdditive.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_31 Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+category"} stable homotopy category
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TheStableHomotopyCategory"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/additive+category"} additive category
              (def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AdditiveCategory"}
            %p
              Hence prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ProductsAreBiproducts"}
              implies that in the stable homotopy category finite coproducts (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wedge+sums"}> wedge sums
              ) and finite products agree, in that they are finite
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/biproducts"} biproducts
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sums"}> direct sums
              ).
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∨
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo ×
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Spectra
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\vee \simeq \times \simeq \oplus \;\;\in \;\; Ho(Spectra)
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_51 Proof
            %p
              By lemma
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StableHomotopyCategoryHasCoproducts"}
              and lemma
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StableHomotopyCategoryIsAbEnriched"}
          %h3#TriangulatedStructure Triangulated structure
          %p
            We have seen
            %a{:href => "#Additivity"} above
            that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+category"} stable homotopy category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ho
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Spectra
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(Spectra)
            is an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/additive+category"} additive category
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homological+algebra"} homological algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/additive+category"} additive category
            one next asks for the existence of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernels"} kernels
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibers"}> fibers
            ) and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cokernels"} cokernels
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibers"}> cofibers
            ) to yield a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pre-abelian+category"} pre-abelian category
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
          %p
            Now here in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"} stable homotopy theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fibers"} homotopy fibers
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+cofibers"} homotopy cofibers
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+categories"} model categories
            was the topic of the general discussion in the section
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "#Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#HomotopyFibers"} Homotopy theory – Homotopy fibers
            %em
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#LongSequences"} Homotopy theory – Long sequences
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#HomotopyPullbacks"} Homotopy theory – Homotopy pullbacks.
            %em stable homotopy theory
            we will find a crucial further property relating homotopy fibers to homotopy cofibers.
          %p
            The axiomatic formulation of a subset of these properties of stable homotopy fibers and stable homotopy cofibers is called a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangulated+category"} triangulated category
            structure. This is the analog in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"} stable homotopy theory
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
            structure in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homological+algebra"} homological algebra
          %table
            %thead
              %tr
                %th
                %th
