                    \\longrightarrow
                    \\Sigma A
                    \\,.
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Schwede12"} Schwede 12, chapter II, theorem 2.9
          .proof
            %h6#proof_52 Proof
            %p
              By prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TheStableHomotopyCategoryIsAdditive"}
              the stable homotopy category is additive, by theorem
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StableModelStructureOnSequentiaSpectraIsStableModelCategory"}
              the functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
              is an equivalence.
            %p The axioms T0 and T1 are immediate from the definition of homotopy cofiber sequences.
            %p
              The axiom T2 is the very characterization of long
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+cofiber+sequences"} homotopy cofiber sequences
              (from
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#LongFiberSequence"} this prop.
            %p Regarding axiom T3:
            %p
              By the factorization axioms of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
              we may represent the morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to A'
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \to B'
              in the homotopy category by cofibrations in the model category. Then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \to B/A
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo ′
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi A
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B' \to B'/A'
              are represented by their ordinary
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibers"} cofibers
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#HomotopyFiber"}> def.
              ,
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#HomotopyFiberIndependentOfChoiceOfFibrantReplacement"} prop.
            %p
              We may assume without restriction (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#RepresentingHomotopyCommutativeSquaresByCommutativeSquares"}> lemma
              ) that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+square"} commuting square
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi ϕ
                                    %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi ϕ
                                    %mi B
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                            %mo ′
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mi f
                                %mo ′
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                            %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A &amp;\overset{f}{\longrightarrow}&amp; B
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{\phi_A}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\phi_B}}
                    \\\
                    A' &amp;\underset{f'}{\longrightarrow}&amp; B'
                    }
            %p
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
              is the image of a commuting square (not just commuting up to homotopy) in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi SeqSpec
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi Top
                        %mi cg
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SeqSpec(Top_{cg})
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi A
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B/A \to B'/A'
              is induced by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
              of ordinary cofibers. To see that this also completes the last vertical morphism, observe that by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+object+argument"} small object argument
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#SmallObjectArgument"}> prop.
              ) we have
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functorial+factorization"} functorial factorization
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#FunctorialFactorization"}> def.
              ).
            %p With this, again the universal property of the ordinary cofiber gives the fourth vertical morphism needed for T3.
            %p
              Axiom T4 follows in the same fashion: we may represent all spectra by CW-spectra and represent
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f'
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ′
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f'\circ f
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+cones"} mapping cones
              as above produces the commuting diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi g
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi h
                          %mtd
                            %mi Σ
                            %mi A
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mo =
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi f
                                  %mo ′
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi x
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mo =
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mi f
                                %mo ′
                                %mo ∘
                                %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mi D
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mi g
                                %mo ″
                          %mtd
                            %mi D
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mi h
                                %mo ″
                          %mtd
                            %mi Σ
                            %mi A
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi g
                                  %mo ′
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 3
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi y
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi D
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi B
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %mi D
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi B
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi h
                                  %mo ′
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi Σ
                                  %mi g
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                  %mo ∘
                                  %mi h
                                  %mo ′
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi Σ
                            %mi B
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mi Σ
                                %mi g
                          %mtd
