                    %msub
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cg
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Spectra
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma\;\colon\;SeqSpec(Top_{cg}) \longrightarrow Ho(Spectra)
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#UniversalPropertyOfHomotopyCategoryOfAModelCategory"}> thm.
              ) of the above commuting squares in the definition of the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+cone"} mapping cone
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibers"} fibers
              by forming
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fibers"} homotopy fibers
              of the bottom vertical morphisms (fibers of fibration replacements, which may be chosen compatibly, either by pullback or by invoking the
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+object+argument"} small object argument
            %p
              First of all, this exhibits the composition of the left two horizontal morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi a
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi \circ a \simeq c
              in the above diagram as the left part (1) of the commuting diagram to be proven.
            %p
              Now observe that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting"} pasting
              composite of the two rectangles on the right of the previous diagram is isomorphic, in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
