                    \&amp;\longrightarrow&amp;
                    \\Sigma X
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              This is because the pasting composite of the bottom squares is isomorphic already in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SeqSpec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cg
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SeqSpec(Top_{cg})
              by the above commuting diagrams for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+cone"} mapping cone
              and the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspension"} suspension
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fibers"} homotopy fibers
            %p Hence the top composite morphisms coincide, by universality of homotopy fibers, with the previous top composite:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
