            %p
              commutes in the stable homotopy category. It remains to see that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
              is an isomorphism.
            %p
              To that end, consider for any
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Spectra
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in Ho(Spectra)
              the image of this commuting diagram, prolonged to the left and right, under the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-functor"} hom-functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
