              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
              itself is an isomorphism.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_12 Remark
            %p
              Prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HomotopyCofiberSequencesAreHomotopyFiberSequencesInSpectra"}
              is the homotopy theoretic analog of the clause that makes a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pre-abelian+category"} pre-abelian category
              into an
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
            %p
              A pre-abelian category is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/additive+category"} additive category
              in which
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibers"} fibers
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernels"}> kernels
              ) and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibers"} cofibers
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cokernels"}> cokernels
              ) exist. This is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
              if the cofiber of the fiber of any morphism coincides with the fiber of the cofiber of that morphism.
            %p Here we see that in stable homotopy theory, whose homotopy category is additive, and in which homotopy fibers and homotopy cofibers exist, the analogous statement is true even in a stronger form: the homotopy cofiber projection of the homotopy fiber inclusion of any morphism coincides with that morphism, and so does the homotopy fiber projection of the homotopy cofiber inclusion.
          %p
            In particular there are long exact sequences of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+groups"} stable homotopy groups
            extending in both directions:
          #StableHomotopyGrouspAsHomsOutOfSphereSpectrum.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma_23 Lemma
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi SeqSpec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cg
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in SeqSpec(Top_{cg})
              be any
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequential+spectrum"} sequential spectrum
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi 𝕊
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\pi_0(X)
                    \\simeq
                    [\mathbb{S}, X]
            %p
              between its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+group"} stable homotopy group
              in degree 0 (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StableHomotopyGroups"}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AdditiveCategory"}
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TheStableHomotopyCategoryIsAdditive"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+category"} stable homotopy category
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TheStableHomotopyCategory"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere+spectrum"} sphere spectrum
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StandardSphereSpectrum"}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %p
              Generally, with respect to the graded hom-groups of def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GradedAbelianGroupStructureOnHomsInTheHomotopyCategory"}
              we have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
