          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              %strong (transition to spectral sequences)
              %br/
              For a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tower+of+fibrations"} tower of fibrations
              of spectra, the long sequences of stable homotopy groups associated with any (co-)fiber sequence of spectra, from prop.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LongExactSequenceOfStableHomotopyGroups"}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+couple"} exact couple
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+sequence+of+a+tower+of+fibrations"} spectral sequence of a tower of fibrations
              is the central tool of computation in
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"} stable homotopy theory
            %p
              We discuss how these spectral sequences arise in the section
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+I"} Interlude – Spectral sequences
            %p
              We discuss in detail the special case of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adams+spectral+sequences"} Adams spectral sequences
              in the section
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+2"} Part 2 – Adams spectral sequences
            %p
          %p
            But for handling any of these spectral sequences it is convenient, or, in many cases, necessary to have multiplicative structure available, induced from a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+smash+product+of+spectra"} symmetric monoidal smash product of spectra
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+1-2"} part 1.2 – Structured spectra
          %h2#References References
          %p We give the modern picture of the stable homotopy category, for which a quick survey may be found in
          %ul
            %li#Malkiewich14
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cary+Malkiewich"}> Cary Malkiewich
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The stable homotopy category
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "http://math.uiuc.edu/~cmalkiew/stable.pdf"} pdf
          %p A classical textbook on stable homotopy theory for “unstructured” spectra is
          %ul
            %li#Adams74
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frank+Adams"}> Frank Adams
              , part III sections 2, 4-7 of
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stable+homotopy+and+generalized+homology"} Stable homotopy and generalized homology
          %p
            For establishing the stable model structure on spectra we use the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield-Friedlander+theorem"} Bousfield-Friedlander theorem
            as discussed in
          %ul
            %li#GoerssJardine96
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Goerss"}> Paul Goerss
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J.+F.+Jardine"} J. F. Jardine
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Simplicial+homotopy+theory"} Simplicial homotopy theory
          %p and as applied for general Omega-spectrification functors in
          %ul
            %li#Schwede97
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefan+Schwede"}> Stefan Schwede
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Spectra in model categories and applications to the algebraic cotangent complex
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uni-bonn.de/people/schwede/modelspec.pdf"} pdf
          %p For the discussion of the stability of the homotopy theory of sequential spectra we follow
          %ul
            %li#Jardine15
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+F.+Jardine"}> John F. Jardine
              , sections 10.3 and 10.4 of
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Local+homotopy+theory"} Local homotopy theory
          %p
            For the definition of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangulated+categories"} triangulated categories
            and a discussion of various equivalent versions of the octahedral axiom the following brief note is useful:
          %ul
            %li#Hubery
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrew+Hubery"}> Andrew Hubery
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Notes on the octahedral axiom
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://math-www.uni-paderborn.de/user/hubery/static/Octahedral.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            For the discussion of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangulated+category"} triangulated
            structure of the stable homotopy category we follow
          %ul
            %li#Schwede12
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefan+Schwede"}> Stefan Schwede
              , section II.2 of
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Symmetric+spectra"} Symmetric spectra
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uni-bonn.de/~schwede/SymSpec-v3.pdf"} pdf
